    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Updated the condition to get the current page, should be more coherent now.\r\n\r\nFor the behavior when we remove a widget, the main issue is that we do not reset the page when a widget with some refinements is removed. I don't think this is related to the infinite hits in particular (even if the behavior is more problematic for it since we cannot go back if `showPrevious` is disabled).",
    "commit_id": "f6cf349a792f941464e026a04d14ec72573fb551",
    "created_at": "2019-09-18T13:01:58Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -242,20 +247,11 @@ const connectInfiniteHits: InfiniteHitsConnector = (\n           );\n         }\n \n-        if (!hasShowPrevious) {\n-          return widgetSearchParameters;\n-        }\n-\n-        if (uiState.page) {\n-          // The page in the search parameters is decremented by one\n-          // to get to the actual parameter value from the UI state.\n-          return widgetSearchParameters.setQueryParameter(\n-            'page',\n-            uiState.page - 1\n-          );\n-        }\n+        // The page in the search parameters is decremented by one\n+        // to get to the actual parameter value from the UI state.\n+        const page = hasShowPrevious && uiState.page ? uiState.page - 1 : 0;",
